# Piscine Reloaded: ONE project, ONE Vogsphere repository, ex00 ... ex27 at its
# root. It is a best-of of the Piscine, and most of its tests are the Piscine's
# own, copied from the exercise each one repeats (named beside every call) and
# adapted where the subject differs. Copied rather than referenced, so this
# project stands alone the way every Piscine module does.
#
# It mixes three kinds of exercise, each handled the way the Piscine already
# handles it:
#   ex00-ex05  shell and file turn-ins. The answer is generators/exNN.sh, and
#              deliverable/exNN/ is generated from it and gitignored PER
#              EXERCISE (.gitignore here) -- an archive's permissions and
#              timestamps, and ex05's file name, cannot live in git.
#   ex06-ex23, ex25-ex27  C, headers and programs, written in deliverable/exNN.
#   ex24, ex27 a Makefile.
#
# ft_putchar. The subject: "If ft_putchar() is an authorized function, we will
# compile your code with our ft_putchar.c." Six exercises authorise it (ex06,
# 07, 08, 15, 18, 19). Their stubs declare it -- `void ft_putchar(char c);` --
# and never define it, and every build of their code here links
# tests/ft_putchar.c through `provided_srcs`, as the Moulinette links its own.
# Layers that judge the student's file alone (norm, compile, forbidden,
# prototype, symbols) never see it, so a call to ft_putchar is an authorised
# undefined symbol there, and `write` is not authorised at all. An ft_putchar.c
# turned in by mistake is an extra file, which the files layer fails.
#
# Layers the Piscine runs that are NOT here: c_reference_cost and c_cycles for
# the ft_putchar exercises. Their budgets were measured on answers that call
# write() directly, and a correct answer here pays for one ft_putchar call per
# character; a budget it cannot meet would red correct work.

# Rebuild the generated shell deliverables (ex00-ex05) from the generators:
#   bazel run //c-piscine-reloaded/c-piscine-reloaded:generate
sh_binary(
    name = "generate",
    srcs = ["//tools:generate.sh"],
    args = [package_name()],
)

PUTCHAR = ["tests/ft_putchar.c"]

